WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.040
INTRO:
Beheadings, corruption, dictators,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:08.480
assassinations, human rights violations, and&nbsp;
discrimation. This is often the visual that is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:13.440
painted about Saudi Arabia by the western&nbsp;
media. While it may seem hard to believe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:18.320
many of these characteristics are indeed accurate&nbsp;
when it comes to Saudi Arabia, but like with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:24.640
most things in life, there’s another side to the&nbsp;
story. For many, Saudi Arabia represents culture,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:30.160
history, values, and most importantly&nbsp;
opportunity. I know that for many of us,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:34.080
these positive attributes don’t even come&nbsp;
close to making up for the negative attributes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:41.120
However, there’s millions of people who don’t&nbsp;
quite agree. In fact, Saudi Arabia is home to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:46.480
the third largest immigrant population in&nbsp;
the world coming in at 13.5 million people.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:52.480
Only the US and Germany have a higher immigrant&nbsp;
population. Not only does Saudi Arabia have a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:57.680
large number of immigrants, but they also have&nbsp;
one of the highest immigrants to population ratios&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:03.200
as well. Saudi Arabia’s total population&nbsp;
current stands at just under 35 million people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:09.760
which means that 38.65% of the population is&nbsp;
immigrants. For perspective, immigrants in America&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:16.080
only make up 15.28% of the US population. So,&nbsp;
here’s the untold story of how Saudi Arabia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:25.840
become one of the largest immigration hubs in&nbsp;
the world despite their horrendous reputation.

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:27.840
HARD LABOR:
Starting with the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:33.840
obvious factor, we have jobs. Most people know&nbsp;
that Saudi Arabia is filthy rich off of oil,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:39.200
but they don’t exactly understand the magnitude,&nbsp;
so here’s some numbers to put it in perspective.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:43.600
The biggest company in Saudi Arabia is oil&nbsp;
giant called Saudi Aramco that’s mostly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:48.320
owned by the Saudi government. Contrary to&nbsp;
popular belief, Saudi Aramco was actually the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:55.040
first company in the world to reach a $2 trillion&nbsp;
valuation. In other words, it wasn’t Apple. Also,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.040 --> 00:02:00.160
if you think that companies like Apple and Google&nbsp;
make too much money, just take a look at this.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:04.960
Thanks to elevated oil prices, in the past 12&nbsp;
months, Saudi Aramco boasted earnings of nearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:13.360
a quarter trillion dollars. That’s literally $34&nbsp;
billion more than Apple and Google combined. Also,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:17.920
we should note that Saudi Aramco’s investors don’t&nbsp;
get to keep most of this money like Apple and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:23.200
Google. Saudi Aramco has to hand over roughly half&nbsp;
of their profits straight to the Saudi government.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:28.640
With such numbers, it’s no wonder why the&nbsp;
Saudi government is so rich. But, while these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:34.080
numbers are super glamorous, the same cannot&nbsp;
be said about the lives of Saudi immigrants.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:37.920
The vast majority of Saudi immigrants are&nbsp;
from third world countries that are there to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:43.920
do hard labor. This includes countries like&nbsp;
Egypt, Pakistan, India, Bangladesh, Yemen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:50.400
and Syria. Now, this might be a bit confusing. Why&nbsp;
take all this risk and immigrate to arguably one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:55.520
of the scariest countries in the world just&nbsp;
to be paid minimum wage? Well, the reality&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:58.720
is that these immigrants' lives in&nbsp;
their home countries are simply far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:03.520
worse. Most of them were usually jobless and&nbsp;
couldn’t even afford to carry on daily life.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:08.720
So, Saudi Arabia’s relatively low laborer salaries&nbsp;
actually seem pretty appealing to many of them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:13.440
Technically, Saudi Arabia does have a minimum&nbsp;
wage of 4000 riyals per month or roughly $1000,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:20.000
but this only applies to Saudi citizens, and&nbsp;
immigrants are usually paid less. The average&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:26.000
laborer in Saudi Arabia is paid 36,000 riyals per&nbsp;
year or just under $10,000. Something to note,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:31.200
however, is that companies usually takecare of&nbsp;
housing, food, and other common living expenses.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:36.960
So, it’s actually quite possible to save over&nbsp;
90% of your salary on an annual basis. Also,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:42.000
most immigrants don’t stay here for several years&nbsp;
or decades. They usually come on 3 to 5 year&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:47.840
contracts, save up $25 to $35,000, and head back&nbsp;
home where they now have a small fortune. Take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:53.200
India, for example, where 30,000 American dollars&nbsp;
is equivalent to roughly 2.4 million rupees.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:58.560
This amount of money is basically impossible&nbsp;
to achieve as a hard laborer in India. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:03.360
this is not a small sum of money even for white&nbsp;
collar workers in India like software engineers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:08.080
The average software engineer in India earns&nbsp;
600,000 rupees per year. So, it would take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:12.160
4 years just to earn 2.4 million rupees itself&nbsp;
as a software engineer. If we assume that these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:17.440
engineers could save about 20% of their income, it&nbsp;
would take them 20 years to build up $2.4 million.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:23.440
Now of course, it’s not like these guys will be&nbsp;
stuck at 600,000 rupees per year for 20 years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:27.600
but I think you get the point. For&nbsp;
poor individuals from such countries,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:32.800
taking on a laborer job in Saudi Arabia is&nbsp;
actually super lucrative. But, this money&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:40.040
definitely doesn’t come easy as laborers in Saudi&nbsp;
Arabia are often subject to loads of atrocities.

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:41.840
ATROCITIES:&nbsp;

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:47.840
Starting off with the lighter end&nbsp;
of atrocities, we have overworking.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:52.480
As a hard laborer, it’s extremely unlikely that&nbsp;
you’re only going to be working 8 hours per day.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:57.600
More times than not, you’ll be working ten to&nbsp;
twelve hours for atleast 6 days a week. For&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:03.600
certain industries like the restaurant industry,&nbsp;
these numbers even go up to 16 hours per day. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:07.920
Saudi Arabia does technically have rules that&nbsp;
are supposed to prevent this from happneing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:11.920
For example, working hours aren’t supposed&nbsp;
to exceed 60 hours per week and there are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:17.360
limits to overtime as well. But, if we’re being&nbsp;
honest, it’s not like hard laboreres are gonna&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:22.560
go and report their employers. For them,&nbsp;
they can’t risk losing their jobs or worse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:28.000
their freedom. You see, employers often confiscate&nbsp;
the passports of laboreres as soon as they arrive.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:32.880
And the passports aren’t returned until the term&nbsp;
is over. This ensures that these workers won't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:38.000
try to runaway or report their employers before&nbsp;
their term is over. This too is illegal according&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:43.360
to Saudi law, but that doesn’t mean that it’s&nbsp;
uncommon. Something else that’s pretty common is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:48.960
discrimation. Race and gender based discrimination&nbsp;
is rather common, but just being a laborer itself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:53.520
is usually enough to receive poor treatment. While&nbsp;
none of this is optimal, if you keep your head&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:58.720
down and just do what you’re asked to, you should&nbsp;
be able to complete your term without any issues.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:03.760
But, for some laborers, things take a turn for&nbsp;
the worst. You see, the criminal justice system in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:08.960
Saudi Arabia isn’t exactly fair, so if an employer&nbsp;
reports an laborer for some sort of crime,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:14.240
the laborer is basically screwed. Let’s just say&nbsp;
Saudi Arabia has some questionable ways of getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:18.880
confessions, and they usually have severe&nbsp;
punishments for even the smallest offenses.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:23.600
The ones that are lucky are able to get away with&nbsp;
a couple years in jail and a few hundred lashes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:29.360
but the ones that aren’t so lucky, well they’re&nbsp;
not so lucky. So, it’s best that you stay on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:34.320
good side of your employer regardless of how&nbsp;
big of a douchebag they really are. Given that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:38.640
Saudi Arabia is trying to open up to western&nbsp;
tourists and basically become another Dubai,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:43.760
they have put more effort into fixing these&nbsp;
injustices over the past few years. For example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:48.320
they’ve added stipulations that allow laborers&nbsp;
to switch jobs without their employer’s consent.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.320 --> 00:06:53.200
Similarly, laborers no longer need approval from&nbsp;
their employers to leave or reenter the country.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:56.880
While these are definitely good steps in&nbsp;
the right direction, if laborers don’t take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.880 --> 00:07:01.760
advantage of these opportunities, it doesn’t&nbsp;
really mean anything. Also, just because it’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:06.880
getting better in certain areas doesn’t mean that&nbsp;
it’s getting better in all areas. For example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:12.560
within the first 9 months of 2021, 41 Kenyans died&nbsp;
in mysterious circumstances, and there were over a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:17.840
1000 laborers in distress. Hearing all this, you&nbsp;
probably think that only the most desperate end&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:22.720
up making their way to Saudi Arabia and that’s&nbsp;
true for basically all laborers in the country.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:27.360
But, there is a small portion of immigrants&nbsp;
that come there purely out of free will,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:33.360
and here’s why.
FREE WILL IMMIGRANTS:&nbsp;

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:38.240
While conditions aren’t that great for hard&nbsp;
laborers, the same cannot be said about educated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:44.080
immigrants like engineers, doctors, nurses,&nbsp;
teachers, scientists, and so on. These skills&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:49.920
are highly valued virtually everywhere and it’s&nbsp;
no different in Saudi Arabia. In fact, 85% of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:55.120
engineers in Saudi Arabia are expats, so clearly,&nbsp;
Saudi Arabia is quite appealing for white collar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.120 --> 00:08:00.080
workers as well. Now, it’s not like engineers from&nbsp;
western countries are fighting tooth and nail to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:05.680
try to get into Saudi Arabia. But, the same cannot&nbsp;
be said about engineers from developing countries.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:10.575
Saudi Arabia doesn’t pay insane salaries like&nbsp;
FAANG or something, but they do have white&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.575 --> 00:08:15.280
collar salaries that are basically on par with&nbsp;
most western countries. Take petroleum engineers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:21.680
for example. The average petroleum engineer at&nbsp;
Saudi Aramco earns $109,000 per year. Meanwhile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:28.000
the average petroleum engineer in India earns&nbsp;
811,000 rupees or just about $10,000. Even a top&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:34.080
petroleum engineer in India only earns 4 million&nbsp;
rupees or about $50,000. So, when these engineers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:38.800
are offered a salary that's 2 to 10 times more&nbsp;
than their salaries in India, it’s no wonder why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:43.680
they take the deal. Also, something else that we&nbsp;
should note is that there is no personal income&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:49.040
tax in Saudi Arabia. For Saudi Arabia, it simply&nbsp;
makes more sense to tax a couple of gas companies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:55.840
another 2% than try to tax millions of residents&nbsp;
20 or 30%. With that being said, a $110,000 salary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.840 --> 00:09:01.600
in Saudi Arabia is actually equivalent to about a&nbsp;
$150,000 in America. It’s not just engineers and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:06.720
doctors that are attracted to Saudi Arabia either.&nbsp;
They’re also able to attract a bunch of managers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:12.800
directors, executives, and business leaders.&nbsp;
For example, 18% of CEOs at Saudi companies are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:16.720
actually foreigners. In terms of the living&nbsp;
conditions for these white collar workers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:21.520
they’re obviously way better than hard laborers.&nbsp;
They usually don’t have to worry about employers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:26.960
confiscating their passports or having to work&nbsp;
80 plus hours a week. According to most accounts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:30.880
it seems that life for these workers is very&nbsp;
similar to how life would’ve been if they were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:36.720
in a western country with the same job. There are&nbsp;
of course a few local differences. For example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:40.880
you have regular prayer breaks and you’re&nbsp;
not going to be drinking wine or eating pork,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:45.040
but for the most part, things aren’t all&nbsp;
that different. You shouldn’t mistake these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:49.360
similarities for complete freedom though. If&nbsp;
you break a law, you’re still gonna have a far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:54.560
worse experience than in any western country. But&nbsp;
you know, that’s just part of the deal. If there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:59.840
weren’t any added risks, Saudi Arabia obviously&nbsp;
wouldn’t have to pay as much. So, professional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:05.040
expats don’t tend to stay here for decades either,&nbsp;
but they do tend to stay for longer than laborers.

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:10.000
THE STATE OF SAUDI IMMIGRATION:&nbsp;

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:14.640
In the end, the large number of immigrants&nbsp;
in Saudi Arabia just comes down to one thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:19.280
and that’s jobs. Having world’s largest oil&nbsp;
reserves, it’s only natural that the country&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:24.640
has plenty of opportunities across the board. For&nbsp;
a lot of westerners, these opportunities often&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:28.560
don’t seem to be worth it given the associated&nbsp;
risks of living in the country and the ethical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:33.440
conerns of supporting the country. But, for a&nbsp;
lot of individuals from developing countries,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:38.320
they don’t have the luxury to make such a choice.&nbsp;
Going to Saudi Arabia and grinding out a few years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:43.120
of hard labor is oftentimes the most straight&nbsp;
forward way to escape poverty. Now of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:47.760
the same cannot be said about the white collar&nbsp;
workers. While they may be able to earn a lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:53.040
more in Saudi Arabia, it’s not like they would’ve&nbsp;
starved in their home countries either. So, they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:58.240
did have the luxury of making the choice, and they&nbsp;
chose Saudi Arabia. I know this will probably come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.240 --> 00:11:03.760
of as greedy, unethical, and immoral to many of&nbsp;
you. But, everybody’s experiences and perspectives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:08.560
are different, and you can’t really understand&nbsp;
their situation or reasoning without having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:13.360
lived their lives. But, that’s just what I think.&nbsp;
Would you be willing to work in Saudi Arabia for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:19.040
$200,000 per year? Comment that down below. Also,&nbsp;
drop a like if you hope that labor conditions get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:23.440
better in Saudi Arabia. And of course, consider&nbsp;
checking out our discord community to suggest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.440 --> 00:11:26.880
future video ideas and consider subscribing&nbsp;
